{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e1af35a5ad54fcd5cf93b1acfaebb28f611aedacb1c8350bce273b4903130f13","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_1115ec212031831dbb3cd3af0ac7cb0c22fe6a86b722476f1c14bbb3df9d2f98","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent and well-motivated contribution to the interpretability of neural machine translation. Its primary originality lies in the application of unsupervised cross-model correlation methods to identify and control individual neurons, moving beyond the standard supervised probing paradigm. The work successfully combines existing statistical tools with a novel experimental protocol for translation control, providing concrete evidence for the localized nature of certain linguistic features in NMT models.","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","paper_identity_sha256":"e6247afc8b8bf46b582b35f074d2eb2a71d1ba9c605d28423141d1a0b37926a7","prompt_identity_sha256":"648e54dbeac0695f2b1fad2d7266527c0913a21ac41395efcb7394a6576a9237","raw_response_sha256":"8f67698eb407f511543f21c8bf9648249cdb8d8431c06be2f13ad4d4c00a89cc","request_identity_sha256":"81f6e852e4caca7c6dbe5d221cb15464fecc535cc79ec9bbe4e86501a4d2f01c","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"add01a5133f933d81c362f063222a06d19786d5f332829b0fdf74816ed9c6ee0","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-005"],"review_text":"The paper frames its contribution as addressing the limitations of existing supervised analysis methods by developing unsupervised techniques to analyze individual neurons. It explicitly poses three research questions regarding the importance, interpretability, and controllability of individual neurons in NMT. This formulation is presented as a necessary step to move beyond whole-vector analysis and the dependency on external linguistic annotations, highlighting a specific gap in the current understanding of NMT representation geometry.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-PROB"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011"],"review_text":"The methodology introduces a set of unsupervised ranking methods, including MaxCorr, MinCorr, and LinReg, which are applied to NMT models. While the underlying statistical concepts (Pearson correlation, linear regression) are standard, the paper claims novelty in their specific application to identify important neurons in NMT by leveraging the hypothesis that different models learn similar properties. The paper positions this as a departure from previous NMT analysis that relied on supervised classifiers, though it acknowledges similar approaches in computer vision.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-MTH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-024","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The paper provides original insights into the distribution of linguistic information in NMT models. It demonstrates that specific linguistic properties, such as tense, number, and gender, are captured by individual neurons rather than being fully distributed. The analysis of cross-lingual correlations, particularly the finding that tense neurons in one language correlate with tense neurons in others, offers a new perspective on how NMT models represent grammatical structure. The identification of neurons with complex behaviors, such as activating on numbers only at the beginning of a sentence, further deepens the understanding of model internals.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-ANL"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-029"],"review_text":"The experimental setup involves training 18 NMT models across five language pairs and an auto-encoder to facilitate the cross-model correlation analysis. The paper introduces a specific protocol for controlling translations by modifying neuron activations, which includes steps for tagging, alignment, and success evaluation. This protocol is presented as a new evaluation method for testing the controllability of NMT outputs based on identified linguistic neurons, distinct from standard translation quality metrics.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-012"],"review_text":"The paper combines existing statistical methods (correlation, regression, SVCCA) with the erasure technique to verify neuron importance. The rationale for this combination is that unsupervised methods can identify candidate neurons without external supervision, and erasure can then validate their functional importance. This synergy allows for a more comprehensive analysis than using either method in isolation, as it links the statistical similarity of neurons across models to their actual impact on translation quality.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-COM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper presents results that highlight the limitations of controlling certain linguistic properties, such as gender and number, compared to tense. The low success rates for gender and number control are presented as evidence that these properties are more distributed in the model, making them harder to control via individual neuron modification. This serves as a critical assessment of the extent to which individual neurons can be used for fine-grained control, providing a nuanced view of the localist/distributed debate in NMT.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-NEG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5b381443d5c64defcab1d7773f4ce6252d8fea7d7093d8e1ca14db71fcdd8700","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","paper_ordinal":100,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"8f67698eb407f511543f21c8bf9648249cdb8d8431c06be2f13ad4d4c00a89cc","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"659b7651c6e6618511f5acb65a3f4f119dab4886672a1954b4f47b97351ba9fa","request_identity_sha256":"81f6e852e4caca7c6dbe5d221cb15464fecc535cc79ec9bbe4e86501a4d2f01c","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1046,"prompt_tokens":19033,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20079},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"81f6e852e4caca7c6dbe5d221cb15464fecc535cc79ec9bbe4e86501a4d2f01c","role":"ORIG","role_ordinal":3,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}